  "name": "Reel Diffusion Flow: ncreel as Stock-Flow Dynamics",
  "theory": "primitive-stock-flow",
  "notebook": {
    "cellContents": {
      "b0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001": {
        "tag": "rich-text",
        "id": "b0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
        "content": "# ncreel Diffusion as Stock-Flow\n\nThe entire TUI state modeled as a notcurses_reel(3). Stocks are state quantities (tablet content, focus position, layout allocation). Flows are diffusion processes (noise/denoise at two timescales). The focused tablet is the denoising anchor — reconstructed first at full resolution via focal Kan extension.\n\n## Two-Level Geometry\n- **Inter-tablet**: S^1 cylinder, flat, O(n^2) mixing\n- **Intra-tablet**: Tree hierarchy, 0-hyperbolic, O(log m) mixing\n\n## Gromov Simplification\nM = S^1 x_f T ~QI T. The cylinder is a bounded perturbation. Tree structure dominates asymptotically."
      },
